  "id": "vagal-tone",
  "term": "vagal tone",
  "definition": "Vagal tone, in this psychology context, refers to the level of vagal influence on the heart, commonly reflected by heart rate variability. It is used as a sign of how well neural systems involved in emotion and thinking are functioning, with higher resting levels linked to more adaptive processing of emotional information and better emotion regulation.",
